{
  "requirement": "When stored requirement text differs from the current chapter text, the\n{term}`requirements.ci.validation_error` MUST name the requirement and show a\ncompact line-oriented diff, with `-` for recorded lines and `+` for current lines.\nWhen an outline input's hash differs from its node's current hash, the validation\nerror MUST name the file, the selector, and the node's current line range.\n\n```text\nevidence/requirements.ci.outline_inputs.json: requirement text changed (md/requirements.md:43)\n- Habeas SHOULD check input lines.\n+ Habeas MUST check input lines.\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the sources satisfy `requirements.ci.diagnostics`. The one visible difference is cosmetic, and I judged it acceptable (see the last point).\n\n**Requirement text diff**\n- `validate_evidence_file` (src/evidence.rs) compares the stored text with the current Declaration text. On a mismatch it pushes `\"{label}: {requirement|example} text changed at {source}{diff}\"`.\n- `label` comes from `display_path`, which gives the evidence path, for example `evidence/requirements.one.json`. That path is the requirement's full name, so the error names the requirement.\n- The diff comes from `compact_diff(recorded, current)`. It trims the common prefix and suffix, then emits one `- ` line per recorded line and one `+ ` line per current line. It caps each side at 8 lines and adds a `... N more lines` marker. This is compact and line-oriented, with `-` for recorded and `+` for current, as required.\n- The recorded text is passed as the first argument and the current text as the second, so the markers are the right way round.\n- The same `compact_diff` is reused for changed requirements and definition inputs in `validate_resolved_input`.\n\n**Outline hash diff**\n- `validate_outline_input` emits `\"{label}: outline input changed: {file} {selector|<root>} (now lines {start}-{end}) no longer has the recorded hash\"`.\n- That names the file, the selector, and the node's current line range, which includes attached comments.\n\n**Tests**\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` (src/evidence.rs) asserts `requirement text changed`, `- Old text.`, and `+ First.`. It also asserts the outline error for the root node, `inputs[0]: outline input changed: src/main.rs <root> (now lines 1-2) no longer has the recorded hash`.\n- `outline_inputs_survive_moves_and_unhashed_comments_but_not_edits` (tests/evidence_boundaries.rs) edits a node's code and its doc comment. It asserts the exact messages `src/lib.rs fn[alpha] (now lines 1-2)` and `fn[beta] (now lines 4-6)`. It also asserts that unchanged inputs are not reported and that no diff is printed for hash changes.\n- tests/definitions.rs checks the `input text changed` diagnostic for definition inputs.\n\n**Marking:** `inspect_repository`, `inspect_repository_with_progress`, `book_source_dir`, `validate_evidence_file`, `validate_outline_input`, `validate_resolved_input`, `compact_diff`, and `display_path` all carry `{impl}` markers for this requirement. I found no unmarked code that implements part of it.\n\n**Minor observations (not gaps)**\n- The 8-line cap in `compact_diff` and its multi-line truncation have no dedicated test. The diff behaviour is only asserted on single-line changes. The requirement does not specify a cap, and the function is small.\n- The requirement's illustrative block shows `requirement text changed (md/requirements.md:43)`. The implementation prints `requirement text changed at md/requirements.md:3`. The normative text only asks for the requirement name and the `-`/`+` diff, and the location is still present. I treated this as a cosmetic variation of an illustrative example, not a missing obligation.",
  "inputs": [
